<title>SINGAPORE: Superbowl first half net down nine pct.</title>
<headline>Superbowl first half net down nine pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of S$ unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   3.34   vs   3.68</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	     2.00   vs   2.30</p>
<p>    Turnover			    20.25   vs  15.81</p>
<p>    Other income/interest income   0.09   vs   0.14</p>
<p>    Pre-tax				5.35   vs   5.16</p>
<p>    Tax				    2.07   vs   1.48</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowings	   0.25   vs   0.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	3.81   vs   2.45</p>
<p>Note - Sports and leisure company Superbowl Holdings Ltd said losses were due primarily to new business and items disallowed for tax purposes.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
